# SCSS

Use the modern Sass module system: `@use` and `@forward`. Never use `@import`.

Entry file: `scss/styles.scss`. Compile it with Dart Sass to `assets/css/main.css` and commit the CSS. `style.css` stays the WordPress theme header. PHP enqueues `assets/css/main.css`.

```
scss/
  abstracts/   _variables.scss _colors.scss _mixins.scss _functions.scss _breakpoints.scss
  base/        _reset.scss _typography.scss _global.scss
  layout/      _header.scss _footer.scss _grid.scss
  components/  _button.scss _card.scss _form.scss _hero.scss _navigation.scss
  pages/       _home.scss _single.scss _archive.scss
  utilities/   _helpers.scss _spacing.scss _motion.scss
  styles.scss
```

One component per partial. Add `_product.scss`, `_cart.scss`, and `_checkout.scss` when those views are built.

## Tokens

Components consume custom properties. They do not contain raw hex, font names, or spacing literals. Defaults live in `abstracts/`. The Customizer overrides the properties at runtime.

```scss
@use "../abstracts/colors" as colors;

.button {
  background: var(--color-accent);
  color: var(--color-paper);
  padding: var(--space-s) var(--space-m);
}
```

Default palette, replaced when the Customizer is set: ink `#241816`, paper `#faf6f3`, accent `#8c3d4e`, gold `#a68456`, line `#eadfd6`. Headings use a serif, UI a sans-serif, both stored as custom properties. Enqueue webfonts from PHP.
